{"units": [{"id": "oios_te_eimi-quote1", "translation": "How is it possible to disobey the words of a father?"}, {"id": "oion_tes_esti-orth1", "translation": "it is possible"}, {"id": "oion_tes_esti-def1", "translation": "it is possible"}, {"id": "oion_tes_esti-quote1", "translation": "What mortals are able to drain off these toils for you?"}, {"id": "oion_tes_esti-quote2", "translation": "It is not possible for me either to be silent or not to be silent about these fortunes."}, {"id": "oiosper-orth1", "translation": "of what sort"}, {"id": "oiosper-def1", "translation": "of what sort"}, {"id": "oiosper-quote1", "translation": "He would find a faithful wife in the house, such as he left behind."}, {"id": "oiosper-quote2", "translation": "You have from us such things as are customary."}, {"id": "oiofron-orth1", "translation": "solitary"}, {"id": "oiofron-def1", "translation": "solitary"}, {"id": "oiofron-note1", "translation": "A word not read elsewhere."}, {"id": "oiofron-quote1", "translation": "Solitary, hanging on a vulture-haunted rock."}, {"id": "oistrodegnon-orth1", "translation": "receiving arrows"}, {"id": "oistrodegnon-def1", "translation": "receiving arrows"}, {"id": "oistrodegnon-note1", "translation": "Of a quiver."}, {"id": "oistrodegnon-quote1", "translation": "And this arrow-receiving one."}, {"id": "oistrao_oistreo-orth1", "translation": "to be driven mad"}, {"id": "oistrao_oistreo-orth2", "translation": "to be driven mad"}, {"id": "oistrao_oistreo-def1", "translation": "to be driven mad"}, {"id": "oistrao_oistreo-quote1", "translation": "From there, driven mad, you rushed along the coastal path."}, {"id": "oistrelatos-orth1", "translation": "driven by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrelatos-def1", "translation": "driven by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrelatos-quote1", "translation": "With gadfly-driven terror."}, {"id": "oistrodinetos-orth1", "translation": "whirled around by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodinetos-def1", "translation": "whirled around by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodinetos-quote1", "translation": "Of the gadfly-whirled maiden."}, {"id": "oistrodonetos-orth1", "translation": "shaken by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodonetos-def1", "translation": "shaken by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodonetos-quote1", "translation": "Gadfly-shaken Io."}, {"id": "oistrodonos-orth1", "translation": "shaken by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodonos-def1", "translation": "shaken by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodonos-quote1", "translation": "Of the gadfly-shaken cow."}, {"id": "oistroplex-orth1", "translation": "struck by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistroplex-def1", "translation": "struck by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistroplex-quote1", "translation": "And I, gadfly-struck, am driven."}, {"id": "oistros-orth1", "translation": "gadfly"}, {"id": "oistros-def1", "translation": "gadfly"}, {"id": "oistros-note1", "translation": "See Thesaurus vol. 6 p. 1838."}, {"id": "oistros-note2", "translation": "Thus Turnebus. In M πέδας [fetters], with the inept conjecture adscripted: οἶμαι παῖδες. Ἰνάχου πέλας [I think children. Near Inachus]. Hermannus."}, {"id": "oistros-note3", "translation": "in some manuscripts of Hephaestion and Priscian corrupted into οἶστρος [gadfly]."}, {"id": "oistros-quote1", "translation": "For the horse-fly is born from wood, but the gadfly from the creatures floating in rivers."}, {"id": "oistros-quote2", "translation": "Horse-fly: a certain fly that irritates cattle and drives every animal, but the gadfly only cattle."}, {"id": "oistros-quote3", "translation": "Some gadfly again anoints me, wretched one."}, {"id": "oistros-quote4", "translation": "And the point of the gadfly anoints me, without fire."}, {"id": "oistros-quote5", "translation": "Io, driven by the gadfly."}, {"id": "oistros-quote6", "translation": "CHORUS: The cattle-driving, goading horse-fly. KING: They call it gadfly, those near the Nile."}, {"id": "oistros-word1", "translation": "M πέδας [fetters]"}, {"id": "oistros-word2", "translation": "οἶμαι παῖδες. Ἰνάχου πέλας [I think children. Near Inachus]"}, {"id": "oistros-word3", "translation": "gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodes-orth1", "translation": "gadfly-like, driven as by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodes-def1", "translation": "by which one is driven as by a gadfly"}, {"id": "oistrodes-note1", "translation": "This perhaps should be restored"}, {"id": "oistrodes-note2", "translation": "where in M is ἀζηνίουσιω [with accents erased] μῆνις μάστειρ᾽ ἐκ θεῶν [wrath, avenger from the gods], about which place I spoke above p. 166 b."}, {"id": "oistrodes-quote1", "translation": "O Zeus, the gadfly-like wrath of Io, avenger from the gods,"}, {"id": "oistrodes-word1", "translation": "ἀζηνίουσιω"}, {"id": "oistrodes-word2", "translation": "μῆνις μάστειρ᾽ ἐκ θεῶν [wrath, avenger from the gods]"}, {"id": "oichneo-orth1", "translation": "to go, depart"}, {"id": "oichneo-def1", "translation": "to go, depart"}, {"id": "oichneo-note1", "translation": "Hermann conjectured οἰχνεῖν [to go] for οἰκεῖν [to dwell]."}, {"id": "oichneo-word1", "translation": "to go"}, {"id": "oichneo-word2", "translation": "to dwell"}, {"id": "oichomai-orth1", "translation": "to have gone, to be gone"}, {"id": "oichomai-def1", "translation": "(with imperfect ᾤχόμην and perfect ᾤχωκα) to have gone, to have departed"}, {"id": "oichomai-def2", "translation": "to have perished"}, {"id": "oichomai-quote1", "translation": "Of the Persians who have gone to the land of Hellas."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote2", "translation": "For all the Asian-born strength has gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote3", "translation": "He is gone to the land of the Ionians."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote4", "translation": "But he who escaped is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote5", "translation": "The man is gone, fleeing."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote6", "translation": "And Orestes, the murderer of this mother, is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote7", "translation": "The beast is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote8", "translation": "Such a flower of the Persian land of men is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote9", "translation": "The flower of the Persians is gone, fallen."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote10", "translation": "He is gone, having met with a wrestler."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote11", "translation": "They went, unseen."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote12", "translation": "The race of mortals, dishonored, is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote13", "translation": "Orestes, the hope of the house, is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote14", "translation": "The liquid poured on the ground is gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote15", "translation": "I am gone with fear."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote16", "translation": "With the men who have gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-quote17", "translation": "The fate of those who have gone."}, {"id": "oichomai-word1", "translation": "I had gone"}, {"id": "oichomai-word2", "translation": "I have gone"}, {"id": "oio-orth1", "translation": "to think, suppose"}, {"id": "oio-def1", "translation": "See οἴομαι."}, {"id": "oio-word1", "translation": "to think, suppose"}, {"id": "oionothroos-orth1", "translation": "cried by birds"}, {"id": "oionothroos-def1", "translation": "cried by birds"}, {"id": "oionothroos-quote1", "translation": "A bird-cried lament."}, {"id": "oionoktonos-orth1", "translation": "killing birds"}, {"id": "oionoktonos-def1", "translation": "killing birds"}, {"id": "oionoktonos-quote1", "translation": "A bird-killing storm."}, {"id": "oionopolos-orth1", "translation": "bird-interpreter, augur"}, {"id": "oionopolos-def1", "translation": "one who deals with birds, observer of birds, augur"}, {"id": "oionopolos-quote1", "translation": "If any of the augurs is near."}, {"id": "oionos-orth1", "translation": "bird"}, {"id": "oionos-def1", "translation": "bird"}, {"id": "oionos-note1", "translation": "of Amphiaraus the seer."}, {"id": "oionos-quote1", "translation": "What is this rustling of birds I hear nearby?"}, {"id": "oionos-quote2", "translation": "And the pure air, the path of birds."}]}